From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:18:55 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: widen the dp-port-indexed arrays to the full 0..15
 space

Two arrays are indexed by datapath port id but sized for the four LAN
ports only. Both are safe today purely because their callers gate on
dp_port_id in [2..5]; the moment that gate widens to admit the WAN port
(dp 15) they go out of bounds, and g_cbm_egress_preconfig[] goes out of
bounds on a *write* from the probe-time preconfig loop, into .bss, with
no compiler warning and no runtime check.

Resize them ahead of any gate change so the widening cannot land in the
wrong order:

  - g_cbm_egress_preconfig[6] -> [CBM_MAX_DP_PORTS] (16).
  - CBM_RX_SPPID_MAX 5 -> 15, which sizes g_cbm_rx_netdev[] and, more
    importantly, is the range cbm_rx_set_netdev() enforces. That check
    rejects rather than mis-files, so an unwidened range would leave a
    dp-15 netdev unbound and silently account every WAN frame against
    the default netdev (eth0). g_cbm_rx_mask is already a u32, so
    BIT(15) needs nothing.

16 is silicon, not head-room: the TX descriptor's DW1 ep field is 4 bits
wide, so 15 is the largest dp port the hardware can express.

No functional change - the callers' range gates are untouched here, so
the new slots are unreachable until a later change widens them.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
index c50dcc55d514..ea130e77136d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@ int cbm_hw_init(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-bool g_cbm_egress_preconfig[6];
+bool g_cbm_egress_preconfig[CBM_MAX_DP_PORTS];
 
 extern int hdma_port_enable(int port_id);
 extern int hdma_ig192_toe_dma3_reset(void); /* TOE/DMA3 reset parity */
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.h
index 1f151a4cd11e..d0d24d905863 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.h
@@ -279,6 +279,16 @@ extern struct cbm_buff g_cbm_buff;
 #define SBID_START 16
 #define CBM_NOTFOUND 2
 #define CBM_PORT_MAX 64
+/*
+ * Datapath port-id space on GSWIP-3.0: 0..15. The bound is silicon, not
+ * convention — the TX descriptor's DW1 "ep" field is 4 bits wide
+ * (datapath_api_gswip30.h), so 15 is the largest representable dp port and
+ * any array indexed by dp_port_id needs exactly this many slots. Mirrors
+ * MAX_DP_PORTS in datapath/datapath.h; duplicated rather than included
+ * because the CQM headers deliberately do not pull in the datapath
+ * internals.
+ */
+#define CBM_MAX_DP_PORTS 16
 #ifndef CBM_SUCCESS
 #define CBM_SUCCESS 0
 #endif
@@ -393,7 +403,7 @@ int init_cbm_dqm_cpu_port(int idx);
 void cbm_rx_engine_init(void);
 void cbm_rx_set_netdev(u32 sppid, struct net_device *dev);
 int turn_on_DMA_p2p(void);
-extern bool g_cbm_egress_preconfig[6];
+extern bool g_cbm_egress_preconfig[CBM_MAX_DP_PORTS];
 int setup_eqm_dma_desc(int pid, int desc_count, u32 flags, u32 buf_offset);
 u8 get_lookup_qid_via_index(u32 lookup_idx);
 int cbm_counter_mode_set(int idx, int mode);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_intr.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_intr.c
index 991800bb603e..b3f854eac917 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_intr.c
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ static unsigned long g_cpu_port_alloc;
 static struct tasklet_struct cbm_tasklet[CPU_DQM_PORT_NUM];
 
 #define CBM_RX_SPPID_MIN	2
-#define CBM_RX_SPPID_MAX	5
+#define CBM_RX_SPPID_MAX	15
 #define CBM_RX_SPPID_DEFAULT	5	/* dp5 / eth0 / LAN1 */
 
 static struct net_device *g_cbm_rx_netdev[CBM_RX_SPPID_MAX + 1];
